          "Statement": "ACCEPTED, NOT FIXED: a known CRITICAL finding (CVSS 9.8, stream corruption when server-sent events are used together with view fragments, in Spring MVC and WebFlux) stays in the shipped images until the date below. No fix is available to us. Trivy names 7.0.9 as the fixed version and nothing else, and nothing above 6.2.19 exists on the Spring Framework 6.2 line on Maven Central (checked 2026-11-07), so the fix is a major upgrade, Spring Framework 7 and with it Spring Boot 4, and not a patch. Why it is judged not reachable from this project: there is no SseEmitter, no text/event-stream and no view technology in any src/main, and spring-webflux is in no runtime tree (the evidence is in the matching entry of dependency-check-suppressions.xml, which expires on the same date). Owner and end: issue #303, the Spring Boot 4 upgrade. When it lands, delete this entry and that one.",
