          "Statement": "ACCEPTED, NOT FIXED: a known CRITICAL finding (CVSS 9.8, SSRF and RCE through Spring MVC's XsltView) stays in the shipped images until the date below. No fix is available to us. Trivy names 7.0.9 as the fixed version and nothing else, and nothing above 6.2.19 exists on the Spring Framework 6.2 line on Maven Central (checked 2026-11-07), so the fix is a major upgrade, Spring Framework 7 and with it Spring Boot 4, and not a patch. Why it is judged not reachable from this project: it renders no views at all. It is a JSON API and a set of fake operators, every controller is a @RestController, and nothing resolves a view name, let alone an XSLT one (the evidence is in the matching entry of dependency-check-suppressions.xml, which expires on the same date). Owner and end: issue #303, the Spring Boot 4 upgrade. When it lands, delete this entry and that one.",
